    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "that makes sense. i've also seen some old notes saying there are differences in how different groups experience things like pain or even how certain inflammatory conditions progress. from a clinical standpoint, are there any known physiological differences in how different races respond to medication or manage pain levels? like is it true there are biological differences in pain sensitivity between certain groups?",
